2026-11-13 23:03 Design (worker's choices, provisional with the settings): (1) engine paths exec as bin/skilletor does, so on hook the engine keeps the contract itself; only the starter's own last path is its own: CLI -> one line on stderr, exit 1, bin/skilletor's Node messages verbatim as its first clause; hook -> the same line as {"systemMessage":...} on stdout, exit 0. That differs from bin/skilletor, which exits 1 on hook without Node. (2) cached file <cfg>/skilletor/bin/<version>/skilletor-<version>-<os>-<arch>-<sha256>, PAR dir <that>.par: the pinned checksum is in the name, so a release rebuilt under the same version never runs stale bytes; no re-hash per start. (3) checksum tool looked for before any download; download bounded (curl --connect-timeout 10 --max-time 60, wget -T 10). (4) warmed under the temp name before the rename: a binary whose --version fails is never cached. Hand probe with pp 1.064 (tiny packed script, outside the repo): PAR_GLOBAL_TEMP is used as is (no cache-<sha> subdir), its parent must exist (errno 2 otherwise; the cache dir is it), and the first run after the rename adds only a ~47 KB loader copy, the unpacked set is reused; each download leaves one such copy named .<asset>.<pid>.tmp in the PAR dir. (5) no set -e/-u: -u exits 2, which a UserPromptSubmit hook reads as block.

